  "question": {
    "text": "A hydraulic press can lift <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> when a mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is placed on the smaller piston. It can lift kg when the diameter of the larger piston is increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> times and that of the smaller piston is decreased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> times keeping the same mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;on the smaller piston.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "25600",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Using Pascals law,&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7bf4045f-a1fa-4dd2-9433-e0caa7afa0d4-image.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 136px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> mass can lift <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> in second case then</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>Since</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math> we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>25600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math></p>",
